;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-12, for Phase 17 step 3 (design section
;; 19.3, proposals 1 to 9, approved by the user); reviewed by the user,
;; 2026-10-13. It replaces the file the user reviewed on 2026-10-10,
;; whose Old, New, Register, Close, Read, Write and the string
;; procedures this one keeps or extends. Why this is right:
;; - FileDesc is 1824 bytes under -O2: the control (768) at 0, the block
;;   (512) at 768, name (256) at 1280, registerName (256) at 1536, isNew,
;;   created, open, writable, dirty and byRecord at 1792 to 1797, length,
;;   onDisk and blockStart at 1800, 1804 and 1808, the record pointer at
;;   1812 (its descriptor's one pointer offset), recordStart and
;;   recordLength. A Rider is 16 bytes, as before.
;; - New expands its name with POC_EXPAND_NAME into registerName (the
;;   name itself when that fails, for Create to report); Create makes the
;;   temporary file in registerName's directory, and Register renames it
;;   registerName. NewFile registers every File with
;;   GarbageCollectedHeap.RegisterFinalizer and Finalize, which writes a
;;   dirty block out, closes the file, and erases an unregistered New
;;   file's temporary file by its resultant name (POC_FILE_NAME), ignoring
;;   every status.
;; - Old opens to read (POC_FILE_OPEN); MakeWritable, called by Write and
;;   Purge, creates a New file or closes the file and reopens it to be
;;   written (POC_FILE_REOPEN with 1), a failure going to Fail. Open
;;   reopens a closed file to read (POC_FILE_REOPEN with 0); RecordByte
;;   starts again at the first record after it. Close creates a New file,
;;   flushes, closes, and clears open and writable.
;; - Old looks where the name says when it has ":", "[" or "<", or when
;;   there is no search path; else NextDirectory takes each directory of
;;   searchPath, "~" giving home (SYS$LOGIN) and "~[." merging into it,
;;   and JoinPath puts it before the name, with ":" after a logical name.
;; - Purge writes no bytes at position 0 with POC_FILE_TRUNCATE; GetDate
;;   gives Platform.GetClock's time for a File open to be written, else
;;   POC_FILE_IDENTITY's revision date through Platform.MTimeAsClock;
;;   GetName gives name, or a New file's POC_FILE_NAME, or "".
;; - ReadBytes and WriteBytes go a byte at a time through Read and Write,
;;   after the index check of x[n - 1] when n > LEN(x).
;; - The typed riders' REAL and LONGREAL: FFields, GFields, SingleFields
;;   and DoubleFields take the bytes apart into sign, exponent and a
;;   HUGEINT fraction, VaxToIeee and IeeeToVax adjust them (the exponent
;;   by 2; ShiftRounded's tie to even for denormals; zero, the largest
;;   value and the reserved operand), and the Bytes procedures put them
;;   together. PowerOfTwo shifts a HUGEINT 1, so that 2^52 is not a
;;   LONGINT's ASH under -O2.
;; - Delete, Rename and ChangeDirectory call Platform's Unlink, Rename and
;;   Chdir; the initializer takes MaxPathLength and MaxNameLength from
;;   Platform and home from SYS$LOGIN.
;; - On the guest, vax-files' FilesOut prints guest-run.expected under
;;   -O2 and -OC, as before; vax-files-riders' riders and signed print
;;   what llvm-files-riders' poc prints on Unix, the riders' bytes
;;   included; vax-files-extra's FilesExtra passes its 75 checks.
; Files, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
